      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T23:15:22Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "This test is `TEST_F(ArtdTest, deleteRuntimeArtifactsSpecialChars)`, and as the comment above suggests, its purpose is to verify that `deleteRuntimeArtifacts` doesn\u0027t treat \"*\" as a wildcard.\n\nI think what you suggest is already covered by `TEST_F(ArtdTest, deleteRuntimeArtifacts)`, where I pass `.isa \u003d \"arm64\"` and verify that the files for the ISA is removed. Note that `artd` is agnostic to what \"native ISAs\" are, so any valid ISAs are equivalent to each other in the tests. (You can think that `TEST_F(ArtdTest, deleteRuntimeArtifacts)` tests the non-native ISA case when run on an x86 machine if you feel strongly about the need for testing such a case.)",
